# Approach bring-up of the Pico 74xx tester Rev-B

Rather than soldering everything at once, build in stages and verify each one.

## Stage 1 — Power

Assemble the power section only.
Check for shorts before applying power.
Verify the input voltage.
Measure the regulated outputs:
5.0 V
3.3 V

If those are correct continue to Stage-2
---

## Stage 2 — Pico

Fit the Pico.
Confirm it powers correctly.
Load a simple test program (LED blink or serial output).
Verify communication.

If that is correct continue on to Stage-3
---

## Stage 3 — 74xx Logic

Populate one section at a time.
Check that the logic behaves as expected.
Confirm there are no unexpected current increases.

If that is correct continue on to Stage-4
---

## Stage 4 — Full Functional Test

Run through the intended functionality.
Test a 7400  IC and see if it displays corectly.
If all seems to work ok test some other IC's in tha 74xx family.

## Stage 5 - Your New Work Bench Tester.

